          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are coated fabrics?",
            "answer": "<p>Coated fabrics are textiles finished with a protective polymer coating bonded to a fabric base. The coating creates a smooth, non-absorbent, leather-like surface that is hard-wearing, easy to clean and resistant to stains and water — making coated fabrics a practical upholstery material across many sectors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How are coated fabrics different from real leather?",
            "answer": "<p>Unlike real leather, coated fabrics are animal-free and made to a consistent specification, so colour, texture and performance are uniform across every roll. They offer a leather-like look and feel while being easier to clean, more colour-fast and free from the natural variation and marks found in hides.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are coated fabrics durable and easy to clean?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Coated fabrics are abrasion-resistant and contract-grade, built to withstand heavy use. The non-absorbent surface wipes clean with a mild detergent and resists stains and water, so they stay looking good with minimal maintenance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are they a vegan leather alternative?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — coated fabrics are an animal-free, vegan leather alternative. They deliver the appearance and durability associated with leather upholstery without using any animal materials.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are coated fabrics used for?",
            "answer": "<p>Coated fabrics are specified across healthcare, hospitality, office, marine, automotive, retail, public spaces and more — anywhere upholstery needs to be hard-wearing, easy to clean and resistant to stains and water.</p>"
          }
        },
